      "revision": "complete:1787899938885#1",
      "state_rank": 2,
      "value": "{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"1. Rivers carve valleys and canyons over millions of years.\\n2. The Nile is often considered the longest river in the world.\\n3. Rivers provide fresh water essential for drinking and farming.\\n4. Many major cities have developed along riverbanks for trade.\\n5. Rivers flow downhill, driven by gravity toward oceans.\\n6. Dams on rivers generate hydroelectric power.\\n7. Rivers support diverse ecosystems and wildlife habitats.\\n8. Floodplains created by rivers have fertile soil.\",\"complete\":true}",
